content:
The evidence is now conclusive. E9 shows the bad values originate in the `invoices` table itself, written by invoice-agent. The VAT values are ~6.67x the amount (e.g., 488.64 × 6.67 ≈ 3257.58) rather than 0.15x — this looks like a multiplier of 100/15 = 6.667 instead of 15/100 = 0.15, a classic inverted-fraction bug introduced by the v1.1 "client library upgrade" (E3). The earliest bad row has `created_at=487`, which is after the deploy at t=471 and just before the first anomaly at t=500. Sync-job faithfully copied the bad values (E8 shows invoices and ledger values are identical), so sync-job is not at fault. No investigation needed.

